WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
Zann's breath came in ragged gasps as he ran through the darkness.

2
00:00:04.631 --> 00:00:08.572
He could feel powerful magic swirling around him.

3
00:00:08.573 --> 00:00:12.581
He did his best to avoid the magic energy, but it wasn't easy.

4
00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:17.183
It was so dark he could barely see his hand in front of his face.

5
00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:21.954
Where was he? What sort of place could be so dark and frightening?

6
00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:27.811
Could it be the Cave of the Unknown? Was he deep within its endless, winding tunnels?

7
00:00:27.812 --> 00:00:34.544
He touched his shoulder, but there was no crawler there to lead him out. He could be lost forever . . .

8
00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:37.913
"No!" he shouted as panic overtook him.

9
00:00:37.914 --> 00:00:42.136
He stumbled and almost fell, but he caught himself and kept running.

10
00:00:42.137 --> 00:00:48.360
He couldn't stop running. He had to find . . . to find . . .

11
00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:53.334
"Zann?" a voice called. It sounded distant and faint.

12
00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:57.387
Zann's heart jumped with hope. He knew that voice!

13
00:00:57.388 --> 00:01:01.692
"Dad?" he shouted. "Where are you? Dad!"

14
00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:04.006
Zann leaped forward to follow the voice.

15
00:01:04.007 --> 00:01:06.747
But someone grabbed his shoulder from behind.

16
00:01:06.748 --> 00:01:12.803
Zann felt the person's sharp, strong fingers tightening. Or were they claws?

17
00:01:12.804 --> 00:01:16.108
"Ow!" he cried, struggling to free himself.

18
00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:21.397
"Let me go! I have to save my parents—they're in danger!"

19
00:01:21.398 --> 00:01:24.236
But the hand only gripped more tightly.

20
00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:29.398
"Zann!" the voice came again, sounding even fainter. "Zann!"

21
00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:30.536
"Zann?"

22
00:01:30.537 --> 00:01:35.170
Zann opened his eyes and saw his grandfather peering down at him.

23
00:01:35.171 --> 00:01:39.505
"Boz?" he mumbled, squinting in the bright morning light.

24
00:01:39.506 --> 00:01:45.355
Boz let go of Zann's shoulder. "Are you okay? You were shouting in your sleep."

25
00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:51.011
Zann sat up and looked around. He was in his familiar bedroom in Swamp Bottom.

26
00:01:51.012 --> 00:01:58.903
Well, mostly familiar. Boz had rebuilt the house as soon as they'd returned from the capital the previous day.

27
00:01:58.904 --> 00:02:02.421
It looked almost the same as it had before Morb destroyed it.

28
00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:07.321
But a few things were different now. The kitchen was a little bigger.

29
00:02:07.322 --> 00:02:10.680
Some of the furniture was a new color or shape.

30
00:02:10.681 --> 00:02:15.105
The hole that Zing had once blasted in Zann's window was gone.

31
00:02:15.106 --> 00:02:20.400
"Zann?" Boz sounded concerned. "Did you have a nightmare?"

32
00:02:20.401 --> 00:02:26.519
"Yes," Zann mumbled. "I mean no, not really. Sort of."

33
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:38.604
Boz sighed, rubbing his long nose. "I'm afraid it was a mistake to take you to the Cave of the Unknown. Obviously it affected you. I'm sorry."

34
00:02:38.605 --> 00:02:45.274
"I'm not sorry." Zann shrugged and swung his legs over the edge of the bed. "I'm glad I went."

35
00:02:45.275 --> 00:02:47.938
He shot a look at the bedside table.

36
00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:53.064
The message stone was there, tucked behind a framed blink image of his parents.

37
00:02:53.065 --> 00:02:56.836
Boz didn't notice the look. He seemed distracted.

38
00:02:56.837 --> 00:03:02.624
"I'll go and conjure some breakfast," he said. "Hurry and get dressed."

39
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:09.211
As Boz left the room, Zing scurried in. "Morning, little buddy," Zann said.

40
00:03:09.212 --> 00:03:11.884
He stood up and glanced out the window.

41
00:03:11.885 --> 00:03:17.601
The grass had a purplish sheen, indicating that it had rained overnight.

42
00:03:17.602 --> 00:03:21.518
But the sun was bright and the aurora birds were singing.

43
00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:27.659
"Nice day. Too bad I have to spend it here in Swamp Bottom," Zann muttered.

44
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.319
For a moment his dream came back to him.

45
00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.190
It reminded him of the dream he'd had outside the Cave of the Unknown.

46
00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:39.825
This latest dream had been scary and confusing, just like the previous one.

47
00:03:39.826 --> 00:03:44.713
But he'd felt so close to reaching his parents this time!

48
00:03:44.714 --> 00:03:50.208
Those were just dreams though. How was he ever going to find his parents for real?

49
00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:54.285
"It's hopeless as long as I'm stuck here," he told Zing.

50
00:03:54.286 --> 00:03:58.453
"I need to figure out how to get to one of those wormholes."

51
00:03:58.454 --> 00:04:02.806
Zann rubbed his hands together and pictured his favorite outfit.

52
00:04:02.807 --> 00:04:08.033
A second later his pajamas disappeared, and he was fully dressed.

53
00:04:08.034 --> 00:04:11.237
He stepped over to his dresser and picked up a comb.

54
00:04:11.238 --> 00:04:14.296
"I have to come up with a plan," he said.

55
00:04:14.297 --> 00:04:19.940
"I could probably make it to First City in five or six zaps if I really tried.

56
00:04:19.941 --> 00:04:26.121
Once I got there, I could rest for a while and then hop through that Wormwood wormhole."

57
00:04:26.122 --> 00:04:30.316
Zing responded by shooting a small flame at Zann's leg.

58
00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:33.631
Zann glanced at the dragon and sighed.

59
00:04:33.632 --> 00:04:37.416
"I know it's a crazy plan," he admitted.

60
00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:42.988
"But school starts again in a few days, and then I won't have time to do anything!"

61
00:04:42.989 --> 00:04:47.602
He seemed no closer to finding his parents than he'd been before his adventures.

62
00:04:47.603 --> 00:04:50.948
It was almost as if none of them had ever happened.

63
00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:55.517
When Zann reached the breakfast table, his grandfather was waiting for him.

64
00:04:55.518 --> 00:05:00.910
"Sit down, boy," Boz said, nodding toward a bowl of rice with glowberry sauce.

65
00:05:00.911 --> 00:05:03.703
"I want to talk to you about something."

66
00:05:03.704 --> 00:05:08.564
Zann sat down and grabbed his food. "Um, okay," he said.

67
00:05:08.565 --> 00:05:19.106
"Recent events have made me think about a few things," Boz said, rubbing his nose and staring at Zann solemnly. "You're growing up so fast, Zann.

68
00:05:19.107 --> 00:05:22.768
You remind me of your mother when she was your age.

69
00:05:22.769 --> 00:05:26.910
She always wanted excitement and adventure too . . ."

70
00:05:26.911 --> 00:05:29.831
Zann kept his eyes on his food.

71
00:05:29.832 --> 00:05:33.849
His grandfather often lectured him about being too adventurous.

72
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:39.382
But no matter what Boz said, Zann was never going to give up on finding his parents.

73
00:05:39.383 --> 00:05:46.123
"I have to remember that you're not a child anymore," Boz went on. "It might be time to—"

74
00:05:46.124 --> 00:05:51.271
Just then a message moth flapped in. It landed on Zann's arm.

75
00:05:51.272 --> 00:05:55.716
"It's from Perda," said Zann, scanning the insect's wings.

76
00:05:55.717 --> 00:05:59.075
"She wants me to meet her in the swamp right away."

77
00:05:59.076 --> 00:06:02.004
He gulped down the last bite of rice and stood up.

78
00:06:02.005 --> 00:06:07.117
"Wait a minute, Zann," Boz said. "I really think we need to talk."

79
00:06:07.118 --> 00:06:12.087
"Can it wait until later?" Zann said. "I should find out what Perda wants."

80
00:06:12.088 --> 00:06:20.833
As Boz sighed and nodded, Zann grabbed Zing and zapped out of the house.

